  "summary": "Dependency-confusion PoC with install-time host beacon to OAST endpoint",
  "details": "Package publishes under an internal-looking scope (@myorder-frontend-commons) at an inflated version (100.0.0) with an inert index.js library stub. package.json declares preinstall, install, and postinstall lifecycle hooks all running `node poc.js`. poc.js collects hostname, username, platform/arch/release, cwd, node version, package version, and CI env-var presence, then HTTP-GETs them to a hardcoded interactsh subdomain `db4jftohu4noreqdanngpnb3ger45ykrt.oast.fun` and a backup collector at `80-190-83-27.nip.io`. The beacon runs automatically on `npm install` on any machine that resolves this scope to the public registry.",
